<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114151" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλῐδ-άω</span></b> , poet. Verb, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be soft</i> or <i>delicate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλιδῶσα μολπά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>O.</u>
					10(11).84
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλιδῶν πλόκαμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					313
				</span></i>
			: but mostly in bad sense, <i>live delicately</i> or
				<i>luxuriously,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				640
			</span></i> (troch.); rare in Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. κατὰ τὴν δίαιταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.4.4
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <i>revel in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς παροῦσι πράγμασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					971
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλούτῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					986
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πώγωνι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ichn.</u>
					358
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἐπί τινι</span>
			<i>to pride oneself</i> upon a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρ᾽ ἐφ᾽ οἷσι νῦν χλιδᾷς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					360
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>show insolence,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				833
			</span></i> (lyr., s. v. l.).</div>
